WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.694
Unit two. Internet Research Skills!

2
00:00:05.678 --> 00:00:10.763
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:10.813 --> 00:00:14.469
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:18.873
Today we learn about Internet Research Skills. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.614 --> 00:00:24.408
Research question. Say it with me. Research question!

6
00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:33.114
Multiple sources. Say it with me. Multiple sources!

7
00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:40.751
Bias. Say it with me. Bias!

8
00:00:44.247 --> 00:00:48.147
Credible. Say it with me. Credible!

9
00:00:51.596 --> 00:00:56.123
Summarize. Say it with me. Summarize!

10
00:00:59.663 --> 00:01:04.063
Paraphrase. Say it with me. Paraphrase!

11
00:01:07.565 --> 00:01:11.848
Plagiarism. Say it with me. Plagiarism!

12
00:01:15.346 --> 00:01:19.982
Bibliography. Say it with me. Bibliography!

13
00:01:23.498 --> 00:01:38.146
A good research question guides me to check multiple sources for information. I watch for bias and choose a credible source. When I summarize or paraphrase, I avoid plagiarism and list every source in a bibliography.

14
00:01:38.196 --> 00:01:41.814
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:48.192
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:48.242 --> 00:01:49.392
Bias!

17
00:01:50.468 --> 00:01:55.751
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:57.023
Plagiarism!

19
00:01:58.224 --> 00:02:05.738
Did you know? Comparing multiple sources helps you spot when one source might have incorrect or biased information!

20
00:02:05.788 --> 00:02:08.016
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:09.073 --> 00:02:18.276
Think and answer. Why is it important to use multiple sources when researching?

22
00:02:18.326 --> 00:02:19.476
Great answer!

23
00:02:20.468 --> 00:02:26.218
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:26.268 --> 00:02:29.359
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

